Z||000000||Groove Champion||10-23-2001||01:26 AM||||It's my understanding that with an LT1 (and V8 Archies kit) That the Motor has to be moved in order to clear the drive belts and such on the LT1. <P>If this is the case , when using an LT1 does the waterpump assembly interfere with the inner fender as it does on a std small block?<P>Just wondering. There is a Lt1 (aluminum head camaro 2 bolt main) Lt1 for sale at my local wreckers.<P>How much extra (is any) does an Lt1 Kit cost? I assume you need longer / and short axles to accomodate the engine move.<P>Archie?<BR>Anyone?<P>GC.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierozilla||10-23-2001||01:59 AM||||The engine doesnt get moved. A hole is cut on the pass side rear wheelwell and the w.pump/crank pulleys/belt are placed there sticking inside the wheelwell between the tire and engine. I believe the water pump is either turned upside down, or you can opt for an electrical w.pump. Archie would know better.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLT1||10-23-2001||07:55 AM||||I could ramble about this here all day.<BR>But better check out my site and read as much as you can. Come back or mail me if you have more questions -K? <P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||10-23-2001||10:57 AM||||Fierozilla..When it's an LT1 the engine does get moved over.<P>Check out FieroLt1's site.<P>It's when you have a standard small block then the engine isn't moved.<P>JM<BR>||||reg||1
